# Slice 296 probe (ABSENT-HEAD-WRITE-NORM): `x: j` defines a named Structure x whose content is `j`; `call: x` executes that
# content (a read of j, no effect), the method goes on and returns its own value.  Entry 7; a wrong value leaves as the
# exit code.
fn: f () int
    int: j 3
    x: j
    call: x
    return: j + 4
end: f
int: code 7
int: v f()
if: v != 7
    code: v
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
